# nl-startup-1: a serving core republishes a deleted daemon.json

discovery/mod.rs now has `OwnedDiscovery` (start(root), publish(&Discovery), release(instance_id)); it keeps the last published
document and a thread (250 ms stat) writes it back, the runtime root included, when the file is missing. It is not used yet:
apply this in native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/lifecycle/real.rs (owned by nr-exthost-node-worker-removal),
`impl DiscoveryPublication`. No Cargo, protocol or compose_flip change. real.rs already imports std::sync::Arc.

1. Replace `DiscoveryPublication::new` and `with_writer` by the three functions below. The `spawn` body is the old
   `with_writer` body unchanged except the `Job::Barrier` arm, written as shown:

    pub fn new(root: PathBuf, base: Discovery, on_fatal: OnFatal) -> Self {
        let owned = Arc::new(discovery::OwnedDiscovery::start(root.clone()));
        let kept = Arc::clone(&owned);
        let write: WriteDocument = Box::new(move |_root, document| kept.publish(document));
        Self::spawn(root, base, write, Some(owned), on_fatal)
    }

    fn with_writer(root: PathBuf, base: Discovery, write: WriteDocument, on_fatal: OnFatal) -> Self {
        Self::spawn(root, base, write, None, on_fatal)
    }

    fn spawn(
        root: PathBuf,
        base: Discovery,
        write: WriteDocument,
        owned: Option<Arc<discovery::OwnedDiscovery>>,
        on_fatal: OnFatal,
    ) -> Self {
        // old with_writer body; in the thread loop:
                        Job::Barrier { withdraw, done } => {
                            if withdraw {
                                // The watch stops putting the file back before the file is removed.
                                let withdrawn = match &owned {
                                    Some(owned) => owned.release(&instance_id),
                                    None => discovery::withdraw(&root, &instance_id),
                                };
                                if let Err(error) = withdrawn {
                                    tracing::error!(%error, "discovery was not withdrawn");
                                }
                            }
                            let _ = done.send(());
                        }
    }

2. Test to add in lifecycle/real_tests.rs (it uses the file's own `template()` and imports):

    #[test]
    fn a_deleted_discovery_file_comes_back_until_the_core_withdraws_it() {
        let root = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();
        let publication = DiscoveryPublication::new(root.path().to_path_buf(), template(), Box::new(|_| {}));
        publication.publish(&DiscoveryState { phase: DiscoveryPhase::Serving, blocked: None, drain_id: None });
        publication.flush();
        let file = discovery::path(root.path());
        std::fs::remove_file(&file).unwrap();
        let deadline = std::time::Instant::now() + std::time::Duration::from_secs(10);
        while !file.is_file() {
            assert!(std::time::Instant::now() < deadline, "the discovery file did not come back");
            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(20));
        }
        publication.withdraw();
        std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(600));
        assert!(!file.exists(), "a withdrawn file is not put back");
    }
